4 true] [17592186334873 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535164 true] [17592186334873 1041 "selection" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334873 1104 #edb/ref 17592186334874 13194139535164 true] [17592186334873 1110 #uuid "5ce05379-5553-53c7-bb01-bb348be4c07a" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334874 1034 "(12i-24j)\\,\\text{in}" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334874 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535164 true] [17592186334874 1111 #uuid "9e271d03-575d-53f7-a911-d28ee31a9ca9" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334875 1034 "(-6i-7j)\\,\\text{in}" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334875 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535164 true] [17592186334875 1111 #uuid "8e2646e7-e672-5a84-8852-c9e0ece6e51d" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334876 1034 "(12i+3j)\\,\\text{in}" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334876 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535164 true] [17592186334876 1111 #uuid "c765db7a-de6c-5e95-ba4f-af2b9dfa5550" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334877 1034 "(8i+9j)\\,\\text{in}" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334877 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535164 true] [17592186334877 1111 #uuid "48a9a561-9eeb-5db0-9aed-453da0fabbd1" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334878 1034 "(-3i+14j)\\,\\text{in}" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334878 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535164 true] [17592186334878 1111 #uuid "3c56c738-07d8-5b3d-993a-44e6b4faf029" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334879 1017 #edb/ref 17592186334880 13194139535164 true] [17592186334879 1089 "q-136442" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334879 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535164 true] [17592186334879 1100 "A particle moves from the origin with an acceleration of $(-2i+j)\\,{\\text{ft/s}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $(4i+j)\\,\\text{ft/s}.$ Find the distance from the particle to the origin after $4$ seconds." 13194139535164 true] [17592186334879 1113 #uuid "de2ee23a-84b8-57f6-8861-b47cf90097b3" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334879 1145 "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=4i+j,\\,a=-2i+j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=4\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(4i+j)(4)+\\frac{1}{2}(-2i+j)(4)^{2} \\\\  & =(16i+4j)+8(-2i+j) \\\\  & =(16i+4j)+(-16i+8j) \\\\  & =12j\\,\\text{ft}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the particle to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|12j| \\\\  & =|12| \\\\  & =12\\,\\text{ft}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334880 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334881 13194139535164 true] [17592186334880 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334882 13194139535164 true] [17592186334880 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334883 13194139535164 true] [17592186334880 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334884 13194139535164 true] [17592186334880 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334885 13194139535164 true] [17592186334880 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535164 true] [17592186334880 1041 "selection" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334880 1104 #edb/ref 17592186334881 13194139535164 true] [17592186334880 1110 #uuid "00372825-97b1-53b1-b8a2-9610496469a0" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334881 1034 "12\\,\\text{ft}" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334881 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535164 true] [17592186334881 1111 #uuid "f763f6bc-176d-59e7-891b-1b97dd76260f" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334882 1034 "\\sqrt{14}\\,\\text{ft}" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334882 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535164 true] [17592186334882 1111 #uuid "9254280c-8276-5f2b-98ab-5514d78cbbb2" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334883 1034 "4\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{ft}" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334883 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535164 true] [17592186334883 1111 #uuid "78d6b874-05fa-527a-b09e-787ab7f097c8" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334884 1034 "\\sqrt{12}\\,\\text{ft}" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334884 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535164 true] [17592186334884 1111 #uuid "3572b64b-bf68-503f-a37d-203121ea9c19" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334885 1034 "8\\,\\text{ft}" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334885 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535164 true] [17592186334885 1111 #uuid "3e6d8e48-1a54-5b49-9eab-92684ee75bd7" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334886 1017 #edb/ref 17592186334887 13194139535164 true] [17592186334886 1089 "q-280521" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334886 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535164 true] [17592186334886 1100 "A delivery drone starts from the point with position vector $(1i+2j)\\,\\text{mi}$ and moves with a constant velocity of $(3i-2j)\\,\\text{mi/h}.$ Determine the distance $(|r|)$ from the drone to the origin after $3$ hours.\n\n$\\,|r|=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{mi}$" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334886 1113 #uuid "c1e61923-44f8-5da3-a12f-75078d76a376" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334886 1145 "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=1i+2j,\\,u=3i-2j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the drone after $t=3\\,\\text{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(1i+2j)+(3i-2j)(3) \\\\  & =(1i+2j)+(9i-6j) \\\\  & =(10i-4j)\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the drone to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|10i-4j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{10}^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{116} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{29}\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334887 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334888 13194139535164 true] [17592186334887 1000 #edb/ref 17592186334889 13194139535164 true] [17592186334887 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535164 true] [17592186334887 1041 "field-1" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334887 1104 #edb/ref 17592186334888 13194139535164 true] [17592186334887 1110 #uuid "f8d4e799-d540-5a73-9421-bb3f497c6e73" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334888 1034 "2\\sqrt{29}" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334888 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535164 true] [17592186334888 1111 #uuid "cc7c3a73-c051-5320-b6d9-d1c742969358" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334889 1034 "10" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334889 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535164 true] [17592186334889 1111 #uuid "322f90ee-5a4e-5818-a81e-012433718bab" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334890 1017 #edb/ref 17592186334891 13194139535164 true] [17592186334890 1089 "q-280533" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334890 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535164 true] [17592186334890 1100 "An object moves from the origin with an acceleration of $(-2i+4j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $(3i+j)\\,\\text{m/s}.$ Find the distance from the object to the origin$(|r|)$ after $2$ seconds.\n\n$\\,|r|=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m}$" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334890 1113 #uuid "bcb455c9-26c8-584d-bb4c-1f9bcb5b3690" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334890 1145 "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=3i+j,\\,a=-2i+4j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the object after $t=2\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(3i+j)(2)+\\frac{1}{2}(-2i+4j)(2)^{2} \\\\  & =(6i+2j)+\\frac{1}{2}(-8i+16j) \\\\  & =(6i+2j)+(-4i+8j) \\\\  & =(2i+10j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the object to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|2i+10j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{10}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+100} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{104} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{26}\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535164 true] [17592186334891